course: dictionary
lesson: 167
title: Agency: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An agency is a business or organisation that does a job for other people. Look at the words around it to find out which kind. «Charities and UN agencies use donations to buy food, medicine, blankets and generators for people in and around Ukraine.» The clue is buy food, medicine and blankets for people: an agency is an organisation that helps others.
explain: «Mila gets a letter from her birth mum once a year, passed on through the adoption agency.» The clue is passed on: the agency is the go-between that carries the letters. Ask yourself what job the organisation does, and your meaning should fit the whole sentence.
explain: Agency can also mean a part of a government that does special work. «Space junk is broken satellites and pieces orbiting Earth very fast, and space agencies track it.» Track means follow and watch, so space agencies are government groups that keep an eye on space.
fact: Agency means a business or organisation that provides a service for other people.
fact: Agency can mean a part of a government that does special work, such as a space agency.
fact: Agency can also mean the power to make your own choices.
fact: A space agency, such as NASA, is America's government agency for space.
fact: A refugee agency, such as UNHCR, runs or supports camps for people who have had to leave their homes.
exercise: «Mila gets a letter from her birth mum once a year, passed on through the adoption agency.» In this sentence, what is an agency? | A place where people sleep | * An organisation that does a job for people | A kind of spacecraft | A letter that is sent by post
exercise: NASA is America's space agency. What kind of agency is it? | * A part of a government that does special work | A business that sells holidays | A shop that sells food | A group of friends who play games
exercise: Agency can mean the power to make your own choices. What does it mean in that sense? | * The power to decide things for yourself | A travel company | A rocket | A kind of food
test: «Charities and UN agencies use donations to buy food, medicine, blankets and generators.» What does agencies mean here? | * Organisations that do a job for people in need | Holidays | Groups of people who give donations only | Blankets
test: Which word means a part of a government that does special work? | Charity | * Agency | Camp | Donation
exam: Which of these is an example of an agency? | A cloud | A river | A pencil | * A travel agency that books holidays
